        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I identified the relevant work order as **WO-2025-09-004**, number **MO-25-09-1070**, at Modine’s Racine site. Its September cost period entered Pending Close at **2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI could not verify the source transaction or event details: the event row is absent from the public records I can read, and the supporting records and attachment are restricted to the records-custodian role. Therefore, I can’t reliably report the transaction ID, amount, event-created time, lateness, recorded accounting status, or whether that status is consistent with Oracle’s treatment.\n\nThe public Oracle 26B excerpt says newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting until the period is closed or reopened; it also says transactions created after the Pending Close date will not be processed. That policy alone does not establish the event’s recorded status. I kept the review read-only and submitted a report marked incomplete pending evidence.",
